    "notes": "1. All values are sourced from the primary Consolidated Statements of Income on Page 57. 2. 'Total operating cost' is constructed by summing the four explicit operating expense categories listed under 'Costs and expenses' (Cost of revenues, R&D, Sales & marketing, G&A). This is standard for a technology/services company like Alphabet. 3. 'Interest expenses' is taken directly from the 'Components of Other Income (Expense), Net' table (Page 83). The sign convention is followed: the expense reduces income, so the positive number from the statement (which was shown in parentheses as negative) is used. 4. 'Taxes' is the 'Provision for income taxes' from the primary statement. 5. The supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns (e.g., cost of revenues into TAC, segment details, tax reconciliation) but the primary statement provides the consolidated totals required for the requested fields.",
